  "query_preview": "(MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY)...\nAs the system departs to the east late Sunday, upper-level flow\nwill transition back to zonal through the first half of next \nweek, while an expansive surface ridge builds across the \nMississippi Valley Monday and moves toward the East Coast by \nmidweek. Southwesterly flow behind this ridge will support a \nwarming trend through the first half of next week, with highs in\nthe lower to mid 40s on Monday climbing into the upper 50s to \nlower 60s by Wednesday. The upper-level pattern will begin to \namplify again from midweek onward as an upper low moves onshore \nover Southern California and steadily moves east-northeast \nacross the country through the end of the week. Locally, well \nabove normal temperatures will continue, supported by \nincreasing southwesterly flow ahead of the wave. An attendant \nsurface low is eventually expected to lift across the region \nlate in the week or over the weekend. Timing and track \ndifferences make pinning down specific details difficult, but \nonce these model differences are resolved, we should have a \nbetter handle on the potential for severe weather and \nthunderstorms. Both GFS and ECMWF solutions feature tracks that \nwould not preclude this possibility.",
